==========================================================================
MOSER-ANGLE LADDER: unit-vector counts of L_t = Z[zeta6, w_t]
  w_t = ((2t-1)+i sqrt(4t-1))/(2t),  disc = sqrt(4t-1).  EXACT integer arithmetic.
==========================================================================
   t  4t-1     disc  #units  stable  transv   notes
   1     3    sqrt3   rank2      --      --   rank-2: = Z[zeta6] (t=1 triangular rosette, 6 units)
   2     7    sqrt7      12     yes       6   sqrt7 rung (THM-421/HYP-2262 radius); Q(sqrt-3,sqrt-7)
   3    11   sqrt11      18     yes      12   <== MOSER lattice (Engel et al.); spindle cos=5/6
   4    15   sqrt15      18     yes      12   
   5    19   sqrt19      12     yes       6   
   6    23   sqrt23      12     yes       6   
   7    27   sqrt27   rank2      --      --   rank-2 collapse: 4t-1=27 keeps w_t in Q(sqrt-3) [count N/A in 4D]
   8    31   sqrt31      12     yes       6   
   9    35   sqrt35      18     yes      12   
  10    39   sqrt39      12     yes       6   
  11    43   sqrt43      12     yes       6   
  12    47   sqrt47      18     yes      12   
  13    51   sqrt51      24     yes      18   
  14    55   sqrt55      12     yes       6   

READING:
 - t=1: rank-2 Z[zeta6], the triangular rosette = 6 unit vectors.
 - rank-4 t: EXACT unit-vector count (box-stable R=5 vs R=8).
   18 = 6 triangular + 12 transverse w_t-units;  12 = 6 triangular + 6 transverse.
 - which discriminants give 18 vs 12:
     18-unit (4t-1): [11, 15, 35, 47]
     12-unit (4t-1): [7, 19, 23, 31, 39, 43, 55]
     other counts  : [(51, 24)]
 - degenerate t (4t-1 square or 3*square) collapse into Q(sqrt-3); not rank-4.
   (4t-1=27 at t=7 => sqrt27=3 sqrt3 => w_7 in Q(sqrt-3): triangular-compatible angle.)
